,"followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-19T18:39:34Z","updated_at":"2026-02-19T18:39:34Z","body":"> I don't have any setup for C# installed which is why I didn't include the changes beicause asked for.\r\n\r\nYou can try making the changes in any text editor and compile with GHA.\r\n\r\nIn any case, any pull request labeled `performance` (especially one affecting core stuff) requires performance testing. Feel free to correct me if I'm wrong.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3929153965/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3930522782","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116493#issuecomment-3930522782","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116493","id":3930522782,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qRwSe","user":{"login":"hsvfan-jan","id":73224846,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczMjI0ODQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73224846?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan","html_url":"https://github.com/hsvfan-jan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-19T22:31:46Z","updated_at":"2026-02-19T22:45:30Z","body":"Nintorch and arkology is this in general what you expected? I updated with a GDScript performance test.\r\n\r\nNote that I already converted to \"Ready for review\" as I hope to test the C# build GH creates here. At least that's how I understood you, arkology.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3930522782/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3931367088","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116493#issuecomment-3931367088","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116493","id":3931367088,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qU-aw","user":{"login":"arkology","id":43543909,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTQzOTA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43543909?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology","html_url":"https://github.com/arkology","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-20T03:16:24Z","updated_at":"2026-02-20T03:16:24Z","body":"Yes, the results you've obtained, as far as I understand, should be sufficient, thank you. Ivorforce can provide more precise feedback – he have more experience and knowledge in optimization and the ability to \"greenlight\" such kind of changes. So feel free to ask him for feedback.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3931367088/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3935840372","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116493#issuecomment-3935840372","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116493","id":3935840372,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qmCh0","user":{"login":"hsvfan-jan","id":73224846,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczMjI0ODQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73224846?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan","html_url":"https://github.com/hsvfan-jan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-20T16:18:56Z","updated_at":"2026-02-20T17:07:38Z","body":"Hm, C# results are a bit weird. Maybe I made a mistake but results look very similar or even slightly worse in the optimized branch. I'm really unfamiliar with C# so maybe that's why.\r\n\r\nC# results\r\nThis PR: 128706 ± 1550 μs\r\nMaster: 126581 ± 967 μs\r\n\r\nScript for testing (⚠️ Note: I used AI to convert my above GDScript to C#)\r\n```\r\nusing Godot;\r\nusing System;\r\n\r\npublic partial class NodeCSharpTwo : Node\r\n{\r\n\tprivate Projection proj = new Projection(\r\n\t\tnew Vector4(1, 5, 9, 13),\r\n\t\tnew Vector4(2, 6, 11, 15),\r\n\t\tnew Vector4(4, 7, 11, 15),\r\n\t\tnew Vector4(4, 8, 12, 16)\r\n\t);\r\n\t\r\n\tpublic override void _Ready()\r\n\t{\r\n\t\tfor (int i = 0; i<30; i++)\r\n\t\t{\r\n\t\t\tulong start = Time.GetTicksUsec();\r\n\t\t\t\r\n\t\t\tfor (int j = 0; j < 10000000; j++)\r\n\t\t\t{\r\n\t\t\t\tfloat det = proj.Determinant();\r\n\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t\t\r\n\t\t\tulong end = Time.GetTicksUsec();\r\n\t\t\tulong elapsed = end - start;\r\n\t\t\t\r\n\t\t\tGD.Print($\"Elapsed time [micro s] = {elapsed}\");\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t}\r\n}\r\n```\r\nBuilt with `scons platform=macos production=yes debug_symbols=yes tests=yes module_mono_enabled=yes`\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3935840372/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3936672074","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116493#issuecomment-3936672074","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116493","id":3936672074,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qpNlK","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-20T19:23:29Z","updated_at":"2026-02-20T19:23:29Z","body":"Just to add to what @clayjohn writes above, be sure to read https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/guidelines/optimization.html which contains much of the reasoning here.\r\n\r\nOptimizing such a determinant might make lots of sense in a hot loop on a GPU for example, but if this is called e.g. a few times a frame on CPU there isn't a compelling case to change on performance grounds (but would e.g. if the result was *more* accurate).\r\n\r\nSo showing some profiles with this showing up as a bottleneck might be the next step, if this truly is hot code.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3936672074/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3936689617","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116493#issuecomment-3936689617","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116493","id":3936689617,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qpR3R","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-20T19:27:41Z","updated_at":"2026-02-20T19:27:41Z","body":"> not including floating point precision differences of course\r\n\r\nFloating point precision differences might actually be relevant here, if the reorganization of the grouping of operations has that effect it would have to be weighed against performance improvements I'd say\r\n\r\nDepending on the compiler optimizations reorganizing floating point operations can have direct effects on the exact results as the floating point standard doesn't require guaranteeing that in cases where the data cannot be represented throughout the operation (hence why FMA is relevant in general)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3936689617/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3936722184","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116493#issuecomment-3936722184","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116493","id":3936722184,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qpZ0I","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-20T19:34:58Z","updated_at":"2026-02-20T19:34:58Z","body":"> Floating point precision differences might actually be relevant here, if the reorganization of the grouping of operations has that effect it would have to be weighed against performance improvements I'd say\r\n> \r\n> Depending on the compiler optimizations reorganizing floating point operations can have direct effects on the exact results as the floating point standard doesn't require guaranteeing that in cases where the data cannot be represented throughout the operation (hence why FMA is relevant in general)\r\n\r\nThe reason I mention floating point precision is that any change to operation order will necessarily change the exact behaviour of the operation due to the limits of floating point precision. But if the only behavioural difference is a slight improvement or loss of floating point precision, then I would ignore it. I want to be clear that only meaningful changes to the behaviour of the function are important. \r\n\r\nA more clear example:\r\n`A * (B + C) * D` will have a slightly different result from `A * B * D + A * C * D`, but that difference should not stop us from using the more optimized version.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3936722184/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3940895968","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116493#issuecomment-3940895968","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116493","id":3940895968,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7q5Uzg","user":{"login":"hsvfan-jan","id":73224846,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczMjI0ODQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73224846?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan","html_url":"https://github.com/hsvfan-jan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-22T12:57:36Z","updated_at":"2026-02-22T12:57:36Z","body":"I'll try to look into if there are reasonable game scenarios where we could see a benefit, thanks for the feedback!","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3940895968/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3941166662","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116493#issuecomment-3941166662","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116493","id":3941166662,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7q6W5G","user":{"login":"hsvfan-jan","id":73224846,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczMjI0ODQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73224846?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan","html_url":"https://github.com/hsvfan-jan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hsvfan-jan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-22T15:13:49Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T13:40:08Z","body":"If I understand the code base correctly, places, where I would've expected some possible hotpaths, e.g. when there are many transforms in 3D, seem to rather use the implementation of `Basis::determinant()`.\r\n\r\n`Projection:determinant()` seems to only be directly used in the test case as a caller (if Xcode shows this correctly to me) https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/a3e84cc2af14aa4cffbefd8e13492e59567a64e3/tests/core/math/test_projection.cpp#L99 or when called directly through GDScript. For the latter, I agree that it's unlikely for someone to call the function that often in a frame.\r\n\r\n[These examples by raylibfan](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/11821#issuecomment-2676278044) from the proposal could be a valid real game scenario:\r\n\r\n> 2. An intersection point of three geometric planes (or triangles or quads) in 3d space;\r\n> 3. An intersection point of one geometric plane (or triangle or quad) and vector (like in raycasting).\r\n> \r\n> In examples 2 and 3 perfomance is the key.\r\n> In 3d game it can be an archer summoning cloud of hundreds of arrow from the sky (like in Path of Exile) or hundreds of archers shoots with one arrow each (like in Total War series). To calculate a position (Vector3) array where all of the arrows hits the 3d-mesh (landscape, or boss, strucrures, e.t.c.) determinant() function can be used hundreds of times per second per mesh triangle (it's normal if to be clear).\r\n\r\nBut even with this example, it won't be as often as in my test script from above. [Calinou noted in the proposal](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/11821#issuecomment-2675822155), however, the CPU cycles this saves might be worth considering for mobile devices where power consumption matters. This probably won't give a smartphone an extra half an hour of more battery time in the mentioned Path of Exile clone, but maybe *some* time.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3941166662/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]